>Oddly enough, I have *4* coaligned temples in this game. I don't know
>if I have the patience for prolonged sacfesting, though.

4 co-aligned temples? Sounds like there is a good chance that one of
those priests is wearing a [CoMR.  Might be a little risky to find out
without killing them all, but with very careful use of free action and
charm monster you should be able to pacify any robe-wearing priest that
you anger with a force-bolt.  If the priest actually has a [CoMR, you
won't be able to calm him down, but you can aquire a powerful pet that
can finish him off without making you a murderer.

The sacfest for Magicbane might not take that long. Your method should
be: Start in a co-aligned temple at max power.  Wear your rings of SD
and FA.  Cast create monster.  Kill hostile monster. Drop on altar.
Sac. repeat until PW < 10. When PW < 10, do a 99s to regrow your PW,
then repeat.  Eat when hungry.

Staying in a co-aligned temple is HIGHLY recommended.  It will protect
you against the chameleon instakill, and most other dangers as well.
It won't shield you against the risk of creating a hostile with a wand
of death or lightning, but that's why you want reflection and magic
resistance in the first place.

